Now it is the lunch break at the office.
I go outside the office.
There is a mobile shop nearby.
I go into that shop.
There is a shopkeeper there.
"Hello, Bhaiya," I say to him.
"Hello Madam," he says.
"What do you want?" he asks me.
I say, "I want a new SIM card."
He asks, "Do you have an old Indian SIM card?"
I say, "No, I do not have an Indian SIM card."
"I only have a Mexican number."
"I want an Indian number now," I say.
"Okay Madam, no problem," he says.
"I have a very good SIM card."
He tells me to sit.
I sit on the chair in the shop.
